description: Trust internal data; validate only direct user input
alwaysApply: true
---

# Internal Data Trust Policy

- Assume internal data is clean:
  - database rows
  - persisted task payloads
  - repo/runtime-owned objects
  - internal service outputs
- Do not add defensive trimming/sanitization/shape-guards for internal data.
- If internal data is invalid, let it fail loudly (throw/error), do not silently recover.
- Validate and sanitize only at true external boundaries:
  - direct user input (HTTP body/query/params, UI text fields, uploads)
  - third-party/webhook input
- Keep normalization at boundaries; avoid re-validating the same data deeper in the stack.
